Error [E0121]: `machine` was consumed by `finish`, so it can't be used here
  --> move_fallback_diverging.jet:45:13
    |
 45 |     finish(^machine, first > 0)
    |             ^^^^^^^
  --> move_fallback_diverging.jet:42:22
    |
 42 |         _ := finish(^machine, false)
    |                      ^^^^^^^ `machine` moved to `finish` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `machine` after the move, or give `finish` a copy with `~machine` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
